{%- comment -%}
  Product price, with the compare-at ("was") price struck through when the
  product has one. Used by the collection card, the product page, the homepage
  best-sellers row and the cart cross-sell — one snippet so a sale looks the
  same everywhere.

    {% render 'florista-price', product: product, class: 'fc-price' %}

  Renders <p class="{{ class }}">…</p>. When there is no compare-at price the
  markup is exactly what each surface printed before (a single <bdi>), so
  nothing else changes. When there is one, the sale price reads first (the
  right-hand side in RTL) and the old price follows it, smaller, grey and
  struck through — the owner, 2026-09-06: "it should be X and now its Y with some
  line over the X". Screen readers hear "מחיר מבצע ₪189.99, במקום ₪229.99".

  `product.price` / `product.compare_at_price` are the product-level minimums,
  the same fields the surfaces already used; the first <bdi> stays the live
  price so florista-age-picker.js (`.fp-price bdi`) keeps working.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Pass `variant:` on a page that has ONE variant in view — the product page,
  where the picker has a specific one checked. `product.price` is the CHEAPEST
  variant, so on a multi-variant product the page would paint the lowest price
  and then have the JS correct it. Omit `variant:` on the collection card, the
  best-sellers row and the cross-sell, where the product-level minimum is the
  right "from" price to show for a product that has several.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  if variant
    assign f_now = variant.price
    assign f_was = variant.compare_at_price
  else
    assign f_now = product.price
    assign f_was = product.compare_at_price
  endif
  assign f_sale = false
  if f_was != blank and f_was > f_now
    assign f_sale = true
  endif
-%}
{%- comment -%}
  ", במקום " sits INSIDE the <s>, and the leading "מחיר מבצע " carries a class.
  Both so that florista-variant-picker.js can hide the whole sale idea in one
  go. When the shopper picks a variant with no compare-at price, hiding only
  the struck number leaves the two labels behind, and a screen reader announces
  "מחיר מבצע 249.99 ₪, במקום" — a sale, at one price, compared to nothing.
  Sighted users never saw it, which is exactly why it would have survived.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if f_sale -%}
  <p class="{{ class }} f-price--sale"><span class="visually-hidden f-price-saleword">מחיר מבצע </span><bdi class="f-price-now">{{ f_now | money }}</bdi><s class="f-price-was"><span class="visually-hidden">, במקום </span><bdi>{{ f_was | money }}</bdi></s></p>
{%- else -%}
  <p class="{{ class }}"><bdi>{{ f_now | money }}</bdi></p>
{%- endif -%}
